From 23a753d456f530b3ee7bd8bb2f6a18077e622872 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 05:17:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 79/98] pvr: reuse the SPM scratch buffer for renders that need
 less

The device keeps one SPM scratch buffer for all render states (only one
partial render runs at a time) but reused it only for a render needing
exactly the same size. Renders of different sizes, as in render to
texture, then freed and allocated a framebuffer-sized buffer every time
they alternated: in glmark2's shadow scene about two 3.6 ms CREATE_BOs
plus the unmap and close per frame. A larger buffer works just as well,
so reuse it when it is big enough.

glmark2-es2 through zink, off-screen 800x600, FPS of two runs each,
before -> after: shadow 66/63 -> 149/149, desktop blur 35/35 -> 50/50,
refract 22/22 -> 27/27, terrain 11/11 -> 12/12.

CTS: TFBC list (9170), dynamic_rendering sample (6745), 5062 list,
synchronization (1718), loops/indexing/graphicsfuzz list (6428):
identical to before.
---
 src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_spm.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_spm.c b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_spm.c
index 4e9f0ba..4b17dd3 100644
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_spm.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_spm.c
@@ -182,9 +182,11 @@ VkResult pvr_spm_scratch_buffer_get_buffer(
     * PR on the whole device until completion.
     * Thus we can safely use the same scratch buffer across multiple
     * framebuffers as the scratch buffer is only used during PRs and only one PR
-    * can ever be executed at any one time.
+    * can ever be executed at any one time. For the same reason a buffer larger
+    * than needed will do: renders of different sizes would otherwise free and
+    * allocate one every time they alternate.
     */
-   if (store->head_ref && store->head_ref->size == size) {
+   if (store->head_ref && store->head_ref->size >= size) {
       buffer = store->head_ref;
    } else {
       VkResult result;
